    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "780018e4-301b-38d3-bb1e-413398667dca",
                "word": "underroot",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "656d1546-c794-320c-9f14-58b14bfe30f0",
                        "entry_id": "780018e4-301b-38d3-bb1e-413398667dca",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Beneath the roots."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b9657be7-6880-47a0-8ffe-9f14e785a5c3",
                                "sense_id": "656d1546-c794-320c-9f14-58b14bfe30f0",
                                "text": "Capillary saturated soil layers in relation to water expenditure are to be divided into three parts: 1) the part above the roots, 2) sucking part-active root part and 3) underroot part."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "186a077e-e3e6-4367-bca3-d59e8806c864",
                                "sense_id": "656d1546-c794-320c-9f14-58b14bfe30f0",
                                "text": "In the ores of Fayzabad region (Central Tajikistan) the crystals of fluorite are only of octohedrial habitus types and it proves that the crystals here represent underroot parts ( according to the scheme of changing the forms of crystals)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "232b605e-5d81-42c4-bfc8-0b7b6e29eb0d",
                                "sense_id": "656d1546-c794-320c-9f14-58b14bfe30f0",
                                "text": "The underroot tendril! We are at fault for giving the invader a path to Lady Brianna."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "d2fff2b6-3a01-395d-8317-ec2f720ef641",
                "word": "underroot",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "3fad408f-8436-47ca-868f-fd7f15596b4d",
                        "entry_id": "d2fff2b6-3a01-395d-8317-ec2f720ef641",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more underroot"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "26c0d824-495d-462d-9297-9fbe71e2d52f",
                        "entry_id": "d2fff2b6-3a01-395d-8317-ec2f720ef641",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most underroot"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "92173822-d934-3ba9-88d6-0a1bb83e6e99",
                        "entry_id": "d2fff2b6-3a01-395d-8317-ec2f720ef641",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Beneath the roots."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ccef7701-8ce5-477c-b9ba-0e02e5d78238",
                                "sense_id": "92173822-d934-3ba9-88d6-0a1bb83e6e99",
                                "text": "It is a rain forest and mucky underroot place where hard land is scarce."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "21e52d15-17e9-4250-b9ea-aa2cc5a12fbc",
                                "sense_id": "92173822-d934-3ba9-88d6-0a1bb83e6e99",
                                "text": "His own bloodveins stretched for the riverroots which...; all held silent communion; all were part of; all tapped the latent elements of seed and death undertree, underroot."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a8d326e0-de43-4d75-8396-cf579710e7f7",
                                "sense_id": "92173822-d934-3ba9-88d6-0a1bb83e6e99",
                                "text": "I already hinted at the problem of sea eutrophication (where excess nutrients cause algae to flourish) due to the phosphates that used to be added to washing powder, and, surely, it is not pleasant for plants to find underfoot (or, better, \"underroot\") those surfactants we use daily at home (please, never pour your dishwater on the roots of a magnificent camellia, even if it is blooming in the garden of a next-door neighbor you cannot stand)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "03546fb0-42db-315b-b70e-a9e2ad6d90ba",
                "word": "underroot",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "c08d9bef-b4c9-42cd-be1b-53d71731e7f6",
                        "entry_id": "03546fb0-42db-315b-b70e-a9e2ad6d90ba",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "underroots"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "75c1d299-753d-3bc2-842f-9702de5020b1",
                        "entry_id": "03546fb0-42db-315b-b70e-a9e2ad6d90ba",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The underground root portion of a plant, or a single underground root."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a2f4080a-c511-4fef-b058-b68000f2fc82",
                                "sense_id": "75c1d299-753d-3bc2-842f-9702de5020b1",
                                "text": "During December limbs and growth in the crown were pruned and an area around the base of the trunk was mulched to help keep the direct underroots frost-free."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9ceffa18-b683-40ae-aea4-ef6878bb6c34",
                                "sense_id": "75c1d299-753d-3bc2-842f-9702de5020b1",
                                "text": "To my knowledge, this is the only tree, having a Manregian underroot, that has shown blackline."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1e4824d2-1d1f-4799-943b-39976ebede0c",
                                "sense_id": "75c1d299-753d-3bc2-842f-9702de5020b1",
                                "text": "The flower stalk has good substance, foliage very similar to P. superbus, rosette has side shoots coming from underroots."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6658d45c-3461-49f0-875d-08e8f31327de",
                                "sense_id": "75c1d299-753d-3bc2-842f-9702de5020b1",
                                "text": "The old man appears in this scene very much like the wise Wotan of Norse myth, who won his wisdom from Mimir's well in the tangled underroots of the World Tree Yggdrasil ."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4a6c39bc-fe6b-3109-b21a-2b85ef1cb121",
                        "entry_id": "03546fb0-42db-315b-b70e-a9e2ad6d90ba",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An underlying root or basis"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "72ea095d-acf0-4453-b0a2-581085134c87",
                                "sense_id": "4a6c39bc-fe6b-3109-b21a-2b85ef1cb121",
                                "text": "The word Bapt cannot here, any more than elsewhere, explain itself, There is nothing back of it. It has no underroot."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "925f21e6-b745-41c0-97fb-966c79e4ef16",
                                "sense_id": "4a6c39bc-fe6b-3109-b21a-2b85ef1cb121",
                                "text": "It has deep underroots."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "99dbb5a7-e187-47e0-92b7-19d1bdaebced",
                                "sense_id": "4a6c39bc-fe6b-3109-b21a-2b85ef1cb121",
                                "text": "But did they check the underroots?” Dash asked, absently looping an arm around Frost and letting her settle in his lap, though his attention was still on the platform. His scaly brow knit in worry. \"It doesn't look stable to me.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "fca7e5dc-f906-34da-b24b-9140a9825eb3",
